                <pb facs="0406" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg308"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hengelmuller to Mr. Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Austro-Hungarian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Bar
                                Harbor</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Adee</hi>: I have received your note of
                    the 9th instant, by which you transmitted to me copies of your correspondence
                    with Mr. Wu with regard to the adoption of measures for the safety and relief of
                    the foreign ministers in Pekin.</p>
                <p>My Government, which has been informed of this exchange of communications by the
                    representative of the United States in Vienna, has desired me to express to you
                    its best thanks for this information and to add that its views on the matter
                    agree entirely with those of the Federal Government.</p>
                <p>Believe me, my dear Mr. Adee, very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hengelmüller.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
